course: dictionary
lesson: 5129
title: Animals without a backbone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An invertebrate is an animal with no backbone. Break the word up: "in-" means "not", and a vertebrate is an animal with a backbone, so an invertebrate is one without. «Animals without a backbone are invertebrates.» The sentence itself gives you the meaning.
explain: Scientists sort animals by their backbones. Vertebrates have backbones: fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals. Every other animal with no backbone is an invertebrate, so the group is very big.
explain: Look for clues in the example sentences. «Insects have six legs and three body parts... while spiders have eight legs and two body parts.» The word "while" shows a contrast, and both animals are invertebrates even though they look different. «Which makes them invertebrates» tells you the reason they are in this group.
fact: An invertebrate is an animal without a backbone.
fact: Most animal species on Earth are invertebrates.
fact: Insects and crabs have hard outer skeletons called exoskeletons.
fact: Snails have shells, and worms have soft bodies.
fact: Jellyfish, octopuses, cuttlefish, sea stars and lobsters are invertebrates, even though they are not fish.
exercise: Which of these animals is an invertebrate? | *Snail | Fish | Frog | Dog
exercise: «Insects have six legs and three body parts.» How many body parts does an insect have? | Two | Eight | *Three | Six
exercise: Leo thinks an octopus must have a backbone because it is so clever. What is true? | *It has no backbone, so it is an invertebrate | It has a backbone, because clever animals always do | It has a backbone, like a dog | It is a fish, so it has a backbone
test: What does "invertebrate" mean? | A mammal that lives in the sea | A bird with no wings | A plant with roots | *An animal without a backbone
test: Which animal is an invertebrate with a hard outer skeleton? | Sparrow | *Crab | Lizard | Trout
exam: Which of these animals has no backbone? | *Jellyfish | Lizard | Eagle | Trout
